```sh
# do this for the first time adding the .env with its psql connection string and prisma directory with its schema.prisma file
bunx prisma init
```

to apply our scheam.prisma changes to the database, we do this

```sh
bunx prisma migrate dev
```

that'll generate a new dir named: migrations in the prisma dir
tutor says, in prod, there's another command instead!!

after being as
model User {
  id Int @id @default(autoincrement())
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  lastName String?
}

we can generate our TS types using the command

```sh
bunx prisma generate
# I think the newer version got it with the prior command, that's what I got by reading
bunx prisma --help
```
*/

model User {
  // singular, it'll become plural User => Users
  id Int @id @default(autoincrement())
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  email String
  hash String

  firstName String?
  // String? as TS means optional
  lastName String?
}

model Bookmark {
  id Int @id @default(autoincrement())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  title String
  description String?
  link String
}

